“THEY’RE NOT PLANTS” (REVISED: WITH PLOT)

Duration: 25 seconds
Style: Cosmic bio-horror, escalation without spectacle
Tone: Discovery → error → containment failure
Aspect: 16:9 cinematic

🚫 ABSOLUTE RULES
NO establishing shots
FIRST FRAME already moving
Average shot: 0.5–0.9s
Max shot: 1.2s
Motion exists in every frame
Biology never “attacks” — it responds intelligently

🎵 MUSIC — RETRIEVAL ONLY (CWPP OK)
🔒 CORE CONSTRAINTS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
Tempo: ~58–64 BPM (slow, predatory, inevitable)
Meter: Free-feeling 4/4 with suspended pulse perception
Key Center: Ambiguous minor (D♯ / E♭ gravity preferred), no functional resolution
Tonality: Microtonal drift allowed; pitch instability encouraged
Dynamic Law: Continuous swell → recoil → swell (never flat, never looping cleanly)
Emotion Rule: Recognition without empathy

🧬 HARMONIC DNA
Static low-register drone built on minor seconds + tritones
Harmonic motion occurs via timbre shift, not chord change
Avoid triads, avoid cadences, avoid tonal comfort
Occasional cluster blooms that fade before resolving

🥁 RHYTHMIC BEHAVIOR
No traditional groove
Pulse implied through:
Low-frequency pressure waves
Breathing-like amplitude modulation
Percussion elements:
Distant, muffled impacts (felt more than heard)
Irregular sub hits that do not repeat evenly
Silence is used as tension, not relief

🎛️ INSTRUMENTATION STACK
Primary Mass:
Analog synth drone (slow LFO pitch wobble, tape-warped)
Organic Intrusion:
Processed string harmonics (bow noise > pitch)
Reversed or stretched vocal textures (genderless, wordless)
Textural Parasites:
High-frequency shimmer artifacts
Metallic resonance tails that feel biological
No Lead Instrument. No Melody Anchor.

🧠 STRUCTURAL PROCEDURE (IMPORTANT)
Phase 1 — Observation (0–90s)
Sparse texture
Drone breathes slowly
Space feels empty but watched

Phase 2 — Recognition (90–210s)
New overtones appear without introduction
Harmonic density increases
Listener feels noticed

Phase 3 — Assimilation (210s–end)
Volume and density peak without climax
Elements blur together
End does not resolve—sound simply withdraws, incomplete

🎚️ PRODUCTION & MIX LAW
Extreme stereo width with unstable center
Low end should feel claustrophobic, not powerful
Reverb tails are long but dirty
Subtle tape hiss and distortion always present
Nothing clean. Nothing sharp. Nothing heroic.

🚫 HARD BANS
❌ No melody hooks
❌ No rhythmic loops
❌ No emotional release
❌ No cinematic “payoff”
❌ No human warmth

🧠 INTENT STATEMENT
This music is not threatening.
It is indifferent.
It does not attack.
It continues.

Low sub-bass pulses begin before first visual.

🔊 SFX PALETTE
Sub-bass heartbeat (irregular)
Wet internal pressure shifts
Suit alarms (muted, partially buried)
Radio static that repeats patterns
Regolith crunch deforming unnaturally

🧬 BIOLOGICAL RULES (IMPORTANT)
Organisms react to:
pressure
vibration
electromagnetic output
They do not move fast
They reconfigure space, not bodies
Growth and relocation occur between cuts
Once triggered, reaction is planetary, not local

🎥 CAMERA LANGUAGE
Helmet cam + over-shoulder fragments
Micro-jitter always present
Camera lags behind events
Focus steals attention at the wrong moments
Peripheral action is more important than center frame

⏱️ SCENE FLOW — WITH STORY
0.0–0.7s
Hard cut — mid-stride, already unstable.
Helmet cam sway.
Blue structures pulsing faintly at the edge of vision.
Heartbeat starts immediately.

0.7–1.4s
Macro snap-cut.
Eye-pods contract as helmet light sweeps.
A faint clicking echo follows the contraction.

1.4–2.2s
Boot hits regolith.
Ground depresses too much.
Biological tissue visible beneath dust.
Astronaut freezes half a step too late.

2.2–3.0s
Hard cut.
The nearest structure tilts toward the footprint, not the astronaut.
As if reading it.

3.0–3.8s
HUD flashes:
SURFACE DENSITY ANOMALY
Radio static spikes — same frequency as the clicking sound.

3.8–5.2s
Rapid montage:
Regolith cracking in branching patterns
Blue tissue seeping upward through dust
Internal nodules rotating, aligning
The moon’s surface is responding as a system.

5.2–6.8s
Astronaut gestures “STOP.”
Second astronaut halts.
The ground continues reacting anyway.

6.8–8.4s
Wide-but-moving shot.
Structures now forming a corridor behind them.

Not closing.
Redirecting.

8.4–10.0s
Suit alarm (low priority, ignored):
NAV PATH RECALCULATING
The map redraws itself incorrectly.

10.0–11.8s
Macro detail:
Blue membrane spreads beneath a communication cable.
Signal strength improves suddenly.

That’s worse.

11.8–13.6s
Radio static resolves into repeating pulses — not language, but timing.
The biology is syncing.

13.6–15.2s
Astronaut turns to look back.
Hard cut before we see what changed.

15.2–17.0s
Tracking shot forward.
Ahead: empty terrain.
Behind (seen only in reflections):
The surface is now fully organic.

17.0–19.2s
Suit HUD escalates:
ENVIRONMENT RECLASSIFIED
Text glitches, reappears as:

BIOSPHERE

19.2–21.5s
The astronauts start moving faster.
The organisms stop reacting.
That’s the most frightening part.

21.5–24.5s
Slow drift forward.
No visible pursuit.
No aggression.

The moon feels awake.

24.6–25.0s — END
Hard cut to black.
Immediate silence.
Ends Cleanly.

Music cuts.

🧠 STORY CLARITY (WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED)
The astronauts triggered a planetary sensory response
The “plants” are interfaces, not organisms
The moon adapted the moment it was stepped on
There is no escape — because there is no enemy